 "thread": "D3BzG5QDcVc",
 "subject": "Generate observeEvent procedurally",
 "messages_listed": 6,
 "last_activity": "2015-04-14T10:02:33Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "VWk_YQH-hs0J",
   "from": "Jean-François Moyen",
   "author": "cf3aa7d5d2624064",
   "date": "2015-04-10T19:50:42Z",
   "subject": "Generate observeEvent procedurally",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Good evening,<br><br>(me again, I&#39;m afraid...)<br><br>I&#39;m now building an interface with several sliders, let&#39;s call them A, B and C for now. In the real app there will be an arbitrary number of them, and their names will be generated by reading a file containing their names -- I&#39;ve been that far. These sliders represent quantities whose sum must always be equal to 100%, so increasing the amount of A should decrease the value of B and C, and this should reflect on the sliders.<br><br>The solution I found so far is to use observeEvent on each slider, and call updateSliderInput from there, and this piece of code works fine:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">observeEvent</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input$sla</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># slider A is called input$sla</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>aa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input$sla<br><br>ee</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input$slb</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input$slc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>names</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ee</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;b&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;c&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>ee_n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ee</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ee</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)*(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">aa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> updateSliderInput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">session</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;slb&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                       value</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">numeric</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ee_n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;b&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> updateSliderInput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">session</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;slc&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                       value</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">numeric</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ee_n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;c&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]))</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    <br>                 <br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">},</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ignoreNULL</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>There may be better way, but this works. When A is moved, B and C change so that the total is kept to 100, and the relative proportion of B to C is preserved.<br><br>Now, I need to generate one such observer for each slider. Relatively easy if there is only a handful of them and if they are known already, but how can I do that for an arbitrary number of sliders ? I tried something like<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">slidernames</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;a&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;b&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;c&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> slidernames</span><span style=\"color:#660\">){</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>observeEvent</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">paste</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;sl&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)]],{</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    <br>   cat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Slider&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;\\n&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Placeholder for more clever stuff,</span><span style=\"color:#800\"> but demonstrates that m is used here too !</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    <br></span></div></code></div><br><br><br>but this does not seem to work (with this example, moving any slider gives &quot;Slider c&quot;, which is not really good...).<br><br>So my immediate question is &quot;how to generate several event observers?&quot;. But I&#39;m willing to take any hint on the larger problem :-)<br><br>With thanks,<br><br>Jeff<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "pVv3fHZYJswJ",
   "from": "Jean-François Moyen",
   "author": "cf3aa7d5d2624064",
   "date": "2015-04-10T19:53:29Z",
   "subject": "Re: Generate observeEvent procedurally",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">PS- and a bonus question is that in fact, slidernames will be a reactive expression...<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">slidernames</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">reactive</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Read from file, parse it, and return a vector with the names of the sliders</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># This vector will be used in a call to renderUI</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br><br><br>so the for().. loop above will not be too happy to try to loop on a reactive value outside a reactive context !<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "VWLXsDRljmAJ",
   "from": "Joe Cheng",
   "author": "ca443e6eaa0e78ed",
   "date": "2015-04-10T20:31:07Z",
   "subject": "Re: Generate observeEvent procedurally",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I suspect your for-loop doesn&#39;t work because the &quot;m&quot; variable is shared across invocations (a weird quirk of R). Can you try it with lapply instead of for?<div><br></div><div>For your bonus question--I think it&#39;d be nice to create the observers at the same time as the sliders.</div><div><br></div><div>slidernames &lt;- reactive({ ... })</div><div>output$sliders &lt;- renderUI({</div><div>  lapply(slidernames(), function(slidername) {</div><div>    observeEvent(input[slidername], {...})</div><div>    sliderInput(slidername, slidername, ...)</div><div>  })</div><div>})</div><div><br></div><div>By the way, if it&#39;s possible for this renderUI to happen more than once, and if it&#39;s possible for the same slidernames to repeat over time, you&#39;ll want to make sure any previously defined observeEvents are suspended. observeEvent() returns an object you can call $suspend() on.</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Apr 10, 2015 at 12:53 PM, Jean-François Moyen <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jfm...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">PS- and a bonus question is that in fact, slidernames will be a reactive expression...<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">slidernames</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">reactive</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Read from file, parse it, and return a vector with the names of the sliders</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># This vector will be used in a call to renderUI</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br><br><br>so the for().. loop above will not be too happy to try to loop on a reactive value outside a reactive context !<br></div></blockquote></div></div>"
