     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>Le vendredi 10 avril 2015 22:31:07 UTC+2, Joe Cheng [RStudio] a écrit :<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I suspect your for-loop doesn&#39;t work because the &quot;m&quot; variable is shared across invocations (a weird quirk of R). Can you try it with lapply instead of for?<div><br></div><div>For your bonus question--I think it&#39;d be nice to create the observers at the same time as the sliders.</div><div><br></div><div>slidernames &lt;- reactive({ ... })</div><div>output$sliders &lt;- renderUI({</div><div>  lapply(slidernames(), function(slidername) {</div><div>    observeEvent(input[slidername], {...})</div><div>    sliderInput(slidername, slidername, ...)</div><div>  })</div><div>})</div><div><br></div><div>By the way, if it&#39;s possible for this renderUI to happen more than once, and if it&#39;s possible for the same slidernames to repeat over time, you&#39;ll want to make sure any previously defined observeEvents are suspended. observeEvent() returns an object you can call $suspend() on.</div></div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Apr 10, 2015 at 12:53 PM, Jean-François Moyen <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">jfm...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">PS- and a bonus question is that in fact, slidernames will be a reactive expression...<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">slidernames</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">reactive</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Read from file, parse it, and return a vector with the names of the sliders</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># This vector will be used in a call to renderUI</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br><br><br>so the for().. loop above will not be too happy to try to loop on a reactive value outside a reactive context !<br></div><span>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Shiny - Web Framework for R&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">shiny-discus...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br></span>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/ccc532a0-cbca-41da-8ae7-fde4a79d5dd2%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/ccc532a0-cbca-41da-8ae7-fde4a79d5dd2%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792399291189000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3DAtyhlhPGjA2C2-b81717\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/ccc532a0-cbca-41da-8ae7-fde4a79d5dd2%40googlegroups.com</a>.<div><div><br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792399291189000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1B_l1eDvHZisiIRaAT-tDL\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</div></div></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n</blockquote></div>"
