     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Friday, April 10, 2015 at 5:08:49 PM UTC-4, Jean-François Moyen wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Joe, a bit late to try in this time zone (bed time !) but it looks rather good. I&#39;ll have a go and let you know, thanks for the hints !!<br><br>Le vendredi 10 avril 2015 22:31:07 UTC+2, Joe Cheng [RStudio] a écrit :<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I suspect your for-loop doesn&#39;t work because the &quot;m&quot; variable is shared across invocations (a weird quirk of R). Can you try it with lapply instead of for?<div><br></div><div>For your bonus question--I think it&#39;d be nice to create the observers at the same time as the sliders.</div><div><br></div><div>slidernames &lt;- reactive({ ... })</div><div>output$sliders &lt;- renderUI({</div><div>  lapply(slidernames(), function(slidername) {</div><div>    observeEvent(input[slidername], {...})</div><div>    sliderInput(slidername, slidername, ...)</div><div>  })</div><div>})</div><div><br></div><div>By the way, if it&#39;s possible for this renderUI to happen more than once, and if it&#39;s possible for the same slidernames to repeat over time, you&#39;ll want to make sure any previously defined observeEvents are suspended. observeEvent() returns an object you can call $suspend() on.</div></div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Apr 10, 2015 at 12:53 PM, Jean-François Moyen <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">jfm...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">PS- and a bonus question is that in fact, slidernames will be a reactive expression...<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;